<!--
    The banks the institute holds its own accounts at.

    Reference data, not demo data. Until now the only Thai banks in the stack
    came from ``kmitl_demo``, which is not installed on a production database,
    so nothing there put a bank behind either the institute's own accounts or a
    payee's — and the e-payment file has to name the bank on both sides.

    ``hooks._seed_bank_accounts`` matches its table against these by BIC to
    attach each paying account to its bank, and that bank is what auto-matching
    compares a payee's own bank against and what the e-payment file names as the
    sending bank.

    The BIC is the key on purpose: it is what the bank export modules themselves
    switch on (``KRTHTHBK`` for KTB, ``SICOTHBK`` for SCB, …), so a record that
    carries the right one is a record those modules already recognise. The demo
    copies carried truncated codes ("KTB", "SCB") that match none of them.

    ``bank_code`` is the bank's clearing code and is seeded here. The e-payment
    layouts write it straight into the file as the receiving bank — KTB's D
    record and SCB's 003 record both do — so an empty one is not "rejected
    visibly" at all: the field goes out as spaces and the bank returns the whole
    file. The four codes are public, fixed, and the same for every customer of
    each bank, so there is nothing for the treasury office to decide.

    ``bank_branch_code`` is still left blank on purpose. It is per branch, not
    per bank, so no single value on a bank record can be right for every payee;
    SCB's layout now takes the receiving branch from the first three digits of
    the payee's own account number instead, which is where SCB puts it.

    ``short_name`` is the treasury office's own everyday abbreviation, read by
    nothing but a human — no bank file uses it. Added later than the rest of
    this record; a database where this file already loaded once needs
    ``hooks._bind_kmitl_bank_data`` to backfill it, since ``noupdate`` means an
    upgrade never re-applies a value added here afterwards.
-->
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="bank_scb" model="res.bank">
        <field name="name">ธนาคารไทยพาณิชย์ (Siam Commercial Bank)</field>
        <field name="bic">SICOTHBK</field>
        <field name="country" ref="base.th" />
        <field name="bank_code">014</field>
        <field name="short_name">SCB</field>
    </record>

    <record id="bank_ktb" model="res.bank">
        <field name="name">ธนาคารกรุงไทย (Krung Thai Bank)</field>
        <field name="bic">KRTHTHBK</field>
        <field name="country" ref="base.th" />
        <field name="bank_code">006</field>
        <field name="short_name">KTB</field>
    </record>

    <record id="bank_bay" model="res.bank">
        <field name="name">ธนาคารกรุงศรีอยุธยา (Bank of Ayudhya)</field>
        <field name="bic">AYUDTHBK</field>
        <field name="country" ref="base.th" />
        <field name="bank_code">002</field>
        <field name="short_name">BAY</field>
    </record>

    <record id="bank_kbank" model="res.bank">
        <field name="name">ธนาคารกสิกรไทย (Kasikorn Bank)</field>
        <field name="bic">KASITHBK</field>
        <field name="country" ref="base.th" />
        <field name="bank_code">004</field>
        <field name="short_name">KBANK</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
